// "[subject] draws N" ([CR#121.1]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT draw — that player
// draws N cards, ONE AT A TIME ([CR#121.2] — a per-card SEQUENCE, NOT a
// simultaneous batch like mill). `Draws`'s slice-family twin of `Draw`: a
// `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit `Composite` named "Draw" whose body
// DESCRIBES the top-of-library → Hand relocation (an `Each` over `TopOfLibrary`,
// `whose: Param(0)`). The engine reads the performer off the body's selection
// and runs the N contained draws SEQUENTIALLY, each binding the library top LATE
// and empty-checking BEFORE its move (an empty library loses the game,
// [CR#120.3,104.3c]).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) rides the body selection's `whose`. The template renders the
// subject context-aware ("Target player draws two cards.", "Each player draws a
// card."); the count spells its noun via the `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Draws(It, 1) (the announced player target / Each-bound player, Jace
// Beleren) / Draws(Target(0), 2).
(
    name: "Draws",
    template: "${0} draws ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Batch(Param(1), Composite(
        name: Draw,
        body: Each(binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: 1, whose: Param(0))), effect: Move(It, Hand)),
    )),
)
